      "writtenOn": "2025-03-07T21:36:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t really understand why an android device would not have a kernel.\n\nTo my knowledge, the aosp_\u003carch\u003e targets cannot really be built/flashed as a real device anymore. I assume you\u0027re either:\n - Inheriting from these in your own product, in which case your product should be adding a kernel.\n - Using them to build apps instead of a whole device.\n\nI think our story for building apps is not really well defined. We need an \"unbundled\" lunch product or something, and in that product we wouldn\u0027t create an android_device module or the filesystem modules at all. In an unbundled build the dexpreopt rules wouldn\u0027t look up the kernel version. Running `m` on an unbundled build would probably need to be an error, requiring you to specify `m MyApp`.",
      "parentUuid": "5bf51a1e_fe528cbe",
      "revId": "ba652d892084416baed07f9905612d1f3ed012e1",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
